#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:2
msgid "An intro to the GUI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:5
msgid "Folder View"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:7
msgid ""
"The left side of the screen shows the ID and current state of all configured "
"folders. Clicking the folder name makes that section expand to show more "
"detailed folder information, and buttons for editing the configuration or "
"forcing a rescan."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:14
msgid "A folder can be in any one of these states:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:16
msgid "Unknown"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:17
msgid "while the GUI is loading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:19
msgid "Unshared"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:20
msgid "when you have not shared this folder,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:22
msgid "Stopped"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:23
msgid "when the folder has experienced an error,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:25
msgid "Scanning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:26
msgid "while Syncthing is looking in the folder for local changes,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:28
msgid "Up to Date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:29
msgid "when the folder is in sync with the rest of the cluster,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:31
msgid "Syncing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:32
msgid "when this device is downloading changes from the network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:34
msgid ""
"Among the folder details, you can see the current \"Global State\" and "
"\"Local State\" summaries, as well as the amount of \"Out of Sync\" data if "
"the the folder state is not up to date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:36
msgid "Global State"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:37
msgid ""
"indicates how much data the fully up to date folder contains - this is "
"basically the sum of the newest versions of all files from all connected "
"devices. This is the size of the folder on your computer when it is fully in "
"sync with the cluster."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:39
msgid "Local State"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:40
msgid ""
"shows how much data the folder actually contains right now. This can be more "
"or less than the global state, if the folder is currently synchronizing with "
"other devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:42
msgid "Out of Sync"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:43
msgid ""
"shows how much data needs to be synchronized from other devices. Note that "
"this is the sum of all out of sync *files* - if you already have parts of "
"such a file, or an older version of the file, less data than this will need "
"to be transferred over the network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:46
msgid "Device View"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:48
msgid ""
"The right side of the screen shows the overall state of all configured "
"devices. The local device (your computer) is always at the top, with remote "
"devices in alphabetical order below. For each device you see its current "
"state and, when expanded, more detailed information. All transfer rates "
"(\"Download Rate\" and \"Upload Rate\") are from the perspective of your "
"computer, even those shown for remote devices. The rates for your local "
"device is the sum of those for the remote devices."
msgstr ""
